# Standards (required)

Follow **docs/tickets/Standards.md** for all UI and flow work. Key rules:

- Required fields use `*` only; never label fields "optional"
- New-user forms start blank; validate inline (not only on submit)
- Dates: **Day DD Mmm YYYY**; time/duration: preset dropdown + custom value
- Address search with suggestions; "add anyway" when no match; home = house icon
- Tags as removable chips with suggestions; typing is secondary
- Destructive/final actions use bottom sheets; share only after save/end
- No developer-only copy in the UI
- Icons come from the `Icon` atom (Phosphor); never hardcode emoji/glyphs as UI icons
- Size icons with the scale tokens (`xs` 16 · `sm` 20 · `md` 24 · `lg` 32 · `xl` 40), e.g. `<Icon name="house" size="xs" />`; avoid raw pixel numbers
- Icon weight follows size automatically (xs/sm → fill, md/lg/xl → bold); allowed weights are regular/bold/fill/duotone (no thin/light), with regular/duotone manual-only (not size-mapped). Only pass an explicit `weight` for semantic exceptions (e.g. an unchecked checkbox or unmet hint stays regular)
- Text comes from the `Text` atom with a `variant` from the type scale (`src/theme/typography.ts`); never hardcode `fontSize`/`fontFamily`/`lineHeight`. One modular scale (base 16, ratio 1.333); Fira Sans headings (`h1`–`h6`), Saira body (`bodyLarge`/`body`/`bodySmall`). Regular + bold available per size via `weight` (headings default bold, body default regular). Roles: `h4` screen titles, `h5` section/sheet titles, `body` copy, `bodySmall` hints/meta

When implementing a flow, read the matching **docs/tickets/Flow/*.md** ticket and update its checkboxes.

Before completing work, run **`npm run check`**.
